---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { CopyScreen } from '../components/Copy/CopyScreen'

const title = 'Morse Code Copy Practice — Code Groups, Words and Callsigns | MorseForge'
const description =
  'Practise copying whole lines of Morse: random five-character code groups, common words, on-air phrases and callsigns. Every line is graded character by character, so you see exactly what you missed.'
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/copy/">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-14">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Copy practice</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Knowing every character and being able to copy a line are different skills. A whole line
      arrives at once here — write down what you got, and see character by character what you
      missed.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <CopyScreen client:load />
    </div>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-line pt-10">
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Why five-character groups?</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Because they cannot be guessed. Real words let you fill in a missing letter from the ones
        either side, which is a useful skill but hides what you can actually hear. Random groups
        measure copying and nothing else, which is why every proficiency test has used them for a
        century. Five is about as much as anyone holds before the next group starts.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">
        Should I write it down or type it?
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Type it here so it can be graded, but the habit worth building is copying a character or two
        <em>behind</em> the sending rather than trying to keep up. Falling behind on purpose is how operators
        reach high speeds — you are decoding the last character while hearing the next.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Working on individual characters instead? Try
        <a href="/practice/" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-4">practice</a>, or the
        <a href="/challenge/" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-4">
          60-second challenge</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
